==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-tempt.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

* {{rhymes|ɛmpt|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|tempter|lang=fro}} (French: ''[[tenter]]''), from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|temptare|lang=la}}, more correctly {{term|tentare||to handle, touch, try, test, tempt}}, frequentative of {{term|tenere||to hold}}. Displaced native {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|costning||temptation|lang=ang}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[provoke]] someone to do [[wrong]], especially by [[promising]] a [[reward]]; to [[entice]].
#: ''She '''tempted''' me to eat the apple.''
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[attract]]; to [[allure]].
#: ''Its glossy skin '''tempted''' me.''
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[provoke]] something; to [[court]].
#: ''It would be '''tempting''' fate.''

